# Copy to `.dev.vars` for `wrangler dev`. NEVER commit the copy.
# For local testing a FAKE token is correct — the suite mints its own initData with it, so no
# real bot credential is needed to exercise every auth path.
BOT_TOKEN="123456:AAH-test-token-not-a-real-one"
ALLOWED_USER_ID="1000000001"

# ── the browser / home-screen way in ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# 🔴 THESE GATE /web/* ONLY. `worker.js` keeps `configuredWeb` separate from `configured` on
# purpose: fold them together and every clone whose .dev.vars predates this block fails the
# TELEGRAM happy path with `401 !== 200` — which trap 1 records as reading exactly like an
# access-control regression, sending you into initdata.js instead of at the missing line.
#
# All four are FAKE, like the two above. The suite mints its own Access tokens against a local
# JWKS and its own session cookies with this key, so no real credential is needed to exercise
# every path — and this repository still carries no personal identifier.
SESSION_SECRET="local-dev-session-signing-key-not-a-real-one"
ALLOWED_EMAIL="someone@example.com"
ACCESS_AUD="0123456789abcdef0123456789abcdef0123456789abcdef0123456789abcdef"
ACCESS_TEAM_DOMAIN="example-team.cloudflareaccess.com"
